WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/driving/components/drivetrain-health/TemperatureGauges.tsx (53 lines):
    FadeIn(delay 0.15) -> GlassPanel(p-6)
      -> <h3 uppercase tracking-wider text-[--text-muted]> <Thermometer/> t('drivetrain.tempGauges','Temperature Gauges')
      -> Grid cols={{default:2, md:4}} of, per sensor:
           <RadialGauge value={value!==null ? convertTempFromSI(value,unit) : 0}
                        max={convertTempFromSI(maxTemp,unit)} label={t(sensor.labelKey, sensor.defaultLabel)}
                        unit={tempUnit} color={tempSeverityColor(value, maxTemp)} />
           <p text-xs text-[--text-muted]> {t('drivetrain.maxLabel','Max')}: {fmtNumber(convertTempFromSI(maxTemp,unit),0)}{tempUnit} </p>
  Hooks (data sources): useTranslation (i18n), useUnits (unitPrefs.temperature in {°C,°F}).
  RadialGauge centre   : fmtNumber(clamped, decimals ?? (Number.isInteger(clamped) ? 0 : getGlobalPrecision()))
                         ; clamped = max(0, min(value,max)); globalPrecision default = 2; fill = clamped/max.
  tempSeverityColor    : null -> #6b7280; ratio=celsius/max; >=.85 critical #ef4444; >=.65 warning #f59e0b; else good #10b981.
                         (Evaluated on RAW Celsius -> unit-independent; the fill is in DISPLAY units, so °F
                          differs from °C — a faithful web quirk reproduced verbatim.)
  Canonical sensors (parent DrivetrainHealthPage.tsx): frontMotor/rearMotor (max 150 °C), inverter (120), battery (60).

